In an HTML document, can add JavaScript in the following ways :-

◉ Inside the <head> or <body> section using <script> tags.
Can place <script> tags in either the <head> or <body> section.

◉ External JavaScript File (Recommended for Larger Scripts)
It store JavaScript in a separate .js file and link to the "src" attribute using <script> tags.
    
◉ Inline JavaScript (Directly in HTML Elements)
It can add small scripts directly in HTML attributes like onclick, onload, ..., etc.
